messages.text:
Now I understand the defect. Looking at `lib/cli/parse.js`:

```js
function parse(argv) {
  if (typeof argv !== 'string') {
    argv = argv.split(' ');  // <-- Fails when argv is an array!
  }
```

The parameter can be either a string or an array per the JSDoc. When it's a **string**, we should split by space. When it's already an **array** (as both failing tests pass), calling `.split()` on it crashes because arrays don't have `.split()`. The condition is inverted: `!== 'string'` should be `=== 'string'`.

